---
/* Privacy policy (T5). Plain language; no legalese theatre. */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — Brimwood Innovation"
  description="How Brimwood Innovation collects, uses, and protects your personal information."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="sec-lede">We collect as little as possible, and we never sell your information.</p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      If you request an introduction, we receive your name, email address, referral
      note, and message. If you join the newsletter, we receive your email address.
      That is all we ask for.
    </p>

    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <p>
      Introduction requests are read by our team so we can respond personally.
      Newsletter addresses receive the newsletter only — every issue carries an
      unsubscribe link, and unsubscribing removes you completely.
    </p>

    <h2>What we never do</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell, rent, or share your personal information with advertisers or
      data brokers. We do not run third-party analytics trackers on this site.
    </p>

    <h2>Where it lives</h2>
    <p>
      Form submissions are processed through our own systems on Cloudflare's
      infrastructure and transactional email is sent via Resend. Both are configured
      to hold only what is needed to operate the site.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask for a copy of the information we hold about you, or ask us to
      delete it, at any time. Email
      <a href="mailto:info@brimwoodinnovation.com">info@brimwoodinnovation.com</a>
      and we will take care of it.
    </p>

    <p><small>Last updated: October 2026.</small></p>
  </div>
</Base>
